1. The Software

"The Software" is everything in this repository: the headers under
include/sw/ (including the generated tables of function addresses, class
layouts, offsets, signatures and constants, and the selection and
arrangement of that data), the sources under src/, the example mods, the
build scripts and the documentation, and any part, copy, translation or
modified version of them.

Not covered by this license: Stormworks: Build and Rescue, its code, its
assets and its name, which belong to their owners and are not part of this
repository; and mods that other people make with the Software, which belong
to their authors (see section 2).

2. What you may do

You may, free of charge and for non-commercial purposes only:

  a. download, read and build the Software;
  b. use the Software to write, build and run your own mods for
     Stormworks: Build and Rescue;
  c. publish and share the mods you made with it, in source or binary form.
     A mod may contain the parts of the Software it needs to build (for
     example the headers it includes), unchanged, together with this
     license file;
  d. fork this repository on the platform where it is published, for the
     sole purpose of proposing changes back to it (pull requests).

3. What you may not do

Unless DeltaV Modding has given you written permission, you may not:

  a. use the Software, or any part of it, to create, publish or distribute
     another SDK, mod loader, modding framework, library, API, header
     collection, binding or tool for making mods of Stormworks: Build and
     Rescue - whether it is a copy, a modified version, a translation into
     another language, a re-implementation built by reading the Software,
     or a work that contains its address tables, layouts, offsets,
     signatures or constants;
  b. extract, copy or re-publish the data of the Software (the address and
     layout tables and the other generated tables), in whole or in a
     substantial part, in any form;
  c. distribute the Software, or a modified version of it, on its own or
     as part of anything other than a mod as allowed in section 2c;
  d. use the Software, or anything made with it, for commercial purposes.
     Commercial means primarily intended for or directed towards commercial
     advantage or monetary compensation;
  e. remove or change this license or the copyright notices;
  f. present your work as made, endorsed or supported by DeltaV Modding.

A mod is not "another SDK" because it offers functions to other mods, as
long as it is published as a mod for players and does not re-publish the
Software or its data (section 3b).

4. End of the permission

The permission of section 2 ends automatically for anyone who breaks this
license. DeltaV Modding may also, at any time, withdraw it from a person by
written notice. Mods published lawfully before the permission ended may
stay published.

